1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,031
In Class 1, you built a mission with one map and one story.

2
00:00:04,931 --> 00:00:06,843
This class is about something larger:

3
00:00:07,293 --> 00:00:09,064
a mission that's a whole galaxy,

4
00:00:09,514 --> 00:00:12,182
with factions, work, a story,

5
00:00:12,632 --> 00:00:15,445
and a game the crew can leave and come back to.

6
00:00:17,245 --> 00:00:19,179
It's called Open Universe.

7
00:00:20,079 --> 00:00:22,681
And the surprising part is how it's made.

8
00:00:23,131 --> 00:00:25,274
All of it comes from one text file,

9
00:00:25,724 --> 00:00:28,157
of the kind you already know how to write.

10
00:00:29,957 --> 00:00:33,137
Today you'll start one, read the file behind it,

11
00:00:33,587 --> 00:00:36,724
and decide what kind of universe you're going to make.

12
00:00:37,924 --> 00:00:41,349
Open Universe is a mission, like Legendary Missions,

13
00:00:41,799 --> 00:00:43,203
so I start it the same way.

14
00:00:44,103 --> 00:00:46,021
I leave the map off the end this time,

15
00:00:46,471 --> 00:00:48,228
because I want the start screen.

16
00:00:50,028 --> 00:00:52,954
Here's a list called Universe, with four on it.

17
00:00:53,854 --> 00:00:55,867
I want The Silver Reach,

18
00:00:56,317 --> 00:00:58,931
which is the one written as an example for writers.

19
00:00:59,831 --> 00:01:03,052
And notice this setting, Start, which says Continue.

20
00:01:03,952 --> 00:01:05,915
A game here is kept between sessions,

21
00:01:06,365 --> 00:01:08,544
and that's half of what this class is for.

22
00:01:09,744 --> 00:01:12,439
This is the system every new game starts in,

23
00:01:12,889 --> 00:01:14,868
and the card calls it Home Port.

24
00:01:15,768 --> 00:01:17,149
There's one station here.

25
00:01:18,049 --> 00:01:20,832
On Comms I select it, and I take a cargo run.

26
00:01:22,632 --> 00:01:24,344
Now the Quest Log, on Helm.

27
00:01:25,244 --> 00:01:28,036
There's the first step of this universe's story,

28
00:01:28,486 --> 00:01:29,742
there's the way to win,

29
00:01:30,192 --> 00:01:31,624
and there's my cargo run.

30
00:01:32,524 --> 00:01:35,022
All three of them send me to another system.

31
00:01:36,822 --> 00:01:38,562
And this is where I have to stop.

32
00:01:39,462 --> 00:01:42,449
In this mission, as it's published today,

33
00:01:42,899 --> 00:01:45,074
the button that makes the jump is switched off.

34
00:01:45,974 --> 00:01:49,289
That's a fault in the mission, and it isn't anything you did.

35
00:01:50,189 --> 00:01:53,201
The mission you make next time has that button on.

36
00:01:54,101 --> 00:01:56,221
So I'll close the game,

37
00:01:56,671 --> 00:01:58,962
and show you the rest from the inside.

38
00:02:00,162 --> 00:02:03,174
Everything about The Silver Reach is in this file.

39
00:02:04,074 --> 00:02:06,198
It's about three hundred and sixty lines.

40
00:02:07,998 --> 00:02:10,852
At the top is one record with a single hash,

41
00:02:11,302 --> 00:02:13,175
and that's the universe itself.

42
00:02:14,075 --> 00:02:17,355
Under it are chapters, each with two hashes.

43
00:02:18,255 --> 00:02:20,789
There are the sides, which are the factions.

44
00:02:21,239 --> 00:02:23,717
There are the jobs their stations offer.

45
00:02:24,617 --> 00:02:26,582
Here's the story, in three steps,

46
00:02:27,032 --> 00:02:30,156
and each step is a quest like the ones you wrote in Class 1.

47
00:02:31,056 --> 00:02:33,865
Then regions and landmarks, which are the map.

48
00:02:34,765 --> 00:02:35,738
And then the people,

49
00:02:36,188 --> 00:02:37,340
and what they say.

50
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:42,210
Each of those chapters is a lecture in this class.

51
00:02:43,410 --> 00:02:46,289
Let me show you one record becoming a place.

52
00:02:47,189 --> 00:02:49,860
This is a side, the Lantern Combine.

53
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:52,422
You can read most of it already:

54
00:02:52,872 --> 00:02:56,253
a heading, a fence, and a fact on each line.

55
00:02:58,053 --> 00:02:59,851
Home is minus four, two.

56
00:03:00,301 --> 00:03:04,200
That's a system, and it's the one the story sends the crew to first.

57
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,808
When a ship arrives there, the game puts a station in it,

58
00:03:10,258 --> 00:03:11,741
named after this side.

59
00:03:12,641 --> 00:03:16,747
This landmark, further down, puts a second station beside it.

60
00:03:17,647 --> 00:03:19,571
And this line, Offers,

61
00:03:20,021 --> 00:03:24,004
is why both stations hand out an escort job and a bounty.

62
00:03:25,804 --> 00:03:28,321
Nobody placed those stations on a map.

63
00:03:29,221 --> 00:03:31,552
The record says where these people live,

64
00:03:32,002 --> 00:03:33,785
and the game does the rest.

65
00:03:34,985 --> 00:03:36,216
Now notice what isn't here.

66
00:03:37,116 --> 00:03:38,622
There's no list of systems.

67
00:03:39,522 --> 00:03:42,129
Nobody wrote the stars, or the nebulas,

68
00:03:42,579 --> 00:03:45,290
or the raiders in the dark between places.

69
00:03:47,090 --> 00:03:50,781
The game makes all of that from one number, called the seed.

70
00:03:51,681 --> 00:03:54,427
The same seed always gives the same galaxy,

71
00:03:54,877 --> 00:03:58,557
so a place you leave is the same place when you come back.

72
00:04:00,357 --> 00:04:02,831
And here's the save, which is tiny.

73
00:04:03,731 --> 00:04:06,248
It holds the seed, where the ship is,

74
00:04:06,698 --> 00:04:08,944
and what the crew has changed.

75
00:04:10,745 --> 00:04:12,433
That's the bargain of this class.

76
00:04:13,333 --> 00:04:16,199
You write the people, the places and the events.

77
00:04:16,649 --> 00:04:17,857
You don't draw the map.

78
00:04:19,057 --> 00:04:20,485
One decision before next time.

79
00:04:21,385 --> 00:04:25,082
Every universe says what kind of game it is, with one word.

80
00:04:26,882 --> 00:04:29,893
Story is one ship, and a tale with an ending.

81
00:04:30,793 --> 00:04:32,427
Campaign is one ship too,

82
00:04:32,877 --> 00:04:34,342
played over many evenings.

83
00:04:35,242 --> 00:04:38,225
Sandbox is an open world with no ending.

84
00:04:39,125 --> 00:04:41,827
And the last two are wars between admirals,

85
00:04:42,277 --> 00:04:43,570
which come late in this class.

86
00:04:45,370 --> 00:04:49,152
For one crew in one ship, the first three play alike today.

87
00:04:50,052 --> 00:04:52,982
So choose the one that's true of what you want to write.

88
00:04:54,182 --> 00:04:55,391
Two things on paper.

89
00:04:56,291 --> 00:04:57,942
First, read the file,

90
00:04:58,392 --> 00:05:00,714
and answer the five questions on the page.

91
00:05:01,614 --> 00:05:03,523
Each answer is one line of it.

92
00:05:05,323 --> 00:05:08,375
Then write three sentences about your own universe:

93
00:05:08,825 --> 00:05:11,125
who lives there, who shoots first,

94
00:05:11,575 --> 00:05:13,769
and what the crew is there to do.

95
00:05:15,569 --> 00:05:18,236
Next time, that page becomes a mission,

96
00:05:18,686 --> 00:05:20,659
and you take it on its first jump.
